00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.690 align:start position:0%
President Vladimir Putin visits Brussels  on january twenty eighth for a summit  focused on the future direction of the  strategic partnership between Russia and  the European Union the summit the 32nd  of its kind will be held in a compact  format with the presidents of the  European Council and Commission the EU  High Representative and russia's Foreign  Minister EU Russia relations have been  going through a challenging period  notably over Ukraine and the union wants  to engage the Russians in a firm and  forward-looking dialogue on the future  of political and economic relations the  talks which will include a short meeting  between the leaders and a working lunch  are likely to focus on the economic  integration plans of both sides in their  shared Eastern European neighborhood  trade issues and key foreign policy  questions like the conflict in Syria and  arounds nuclear program are up for  discussion to the EU with more than 500  million citizens is Russia's biggest  trading partner the talks could also  turn to easing visa requirements for  certain categories of travelers as well  as to European concerns about human  rights and fundamental freedoms in  Russia
 

